  "source": "Same 116 terms, order and categories as v1, copied from the original 'Wine Semantics' notebook (FLAVOR_LEXICON); categories are the notebook's comments, built from the UC Davis Wine Aroma Wheel (Ann Noble). Do not edit: a change requires a new version file.",
  "rule": "Whole-token matching. A review is lower-cased and split into tokens with the regex \\w+ (runs of letters, digits and underscore; hyphens, apostrophes and punctuation separate tokens). A review mentions a term if any of the term's accepted forms is one of its tokens. Forms are the term plus inflections and derivations of the same flavour (plurals, -y/-ed/-ness/-like adjectives and nouns, a few same-flavour compounds and spellings). Excluded: words that contain the term but mean something else (tart, star, breadth, prosecco), tokens that are or contain another lexicon term (pineapple, honeysuckle, acidity), negations (unoaked), proper names and typos. Each form belongs to exactly one term.",
  "notes": "Forms reviewed and approved by the owner on 2026-10-16. v1 (substring matching) stays unchanged in wine_flavor_lexicon_v1.json. The notebook literal lists 'flint' twice (Earthy/Savory and Other); as a Python set it is one term, kept here under its first category.",
